Understand the problem – Clearly identify what needs to be solved.

Generate ideas – Think of multiple possible solutions without judging them immediately.

Explore different perspectives – Consider the needs of users, businesses, technology, cost, etc.

Build on ideas – Combine, modify, or expand existing ideas.

Evaluate ideas – After brainstorming, compare ideas based on feasibility, usefulness, cost, and impact.

Select promising concepts – Choose a few ideas to develop further into prototypes or detailed solutions.
